# greatfallstoolbus.org Bazel Configuration
#
# Bazel 8 + Bzlmod. Mirrors elders.tinyland.dev's two-registry chain:
# tinyland-inc/bazel-registry first, then BCR. Site build remains
# `pnpm run build`; Bazel exists for module-graph integrity proofs.

common --enable_bzlmod
# Supply-chain hardening: pin tinyland-inc/bazel-registry to an immutable
# commit SHA instead of the mutable `main` ref so module metadata
# (MODULE.bazel + source.json) cannot silently change under us. Bump the SHA
# deliberately, in its own commit, with the refresh one-liner:
#   sed -i '' "s|bazel-registry/[0-9a-f]\{40\}|bazel-registry/$(gh api repos/tinyland-inc/bazel-registry/commits/main --jq .sha)|" .bazelrc
#   bazelisk mod graph   # regenerates MODULE.bazel.lock
# The registry README states the rule this repo follows: "A SHA bump must
# land alongside a `MODULE.bazel.lock` refresh in the same commit." Bumping
# the SHA without re-committing the regenerated lock is a broken change.
#
# NOTE (TIN-3857): the SHA pinned below is origin/main of
# tinyland-inc/bazel-registry taken AFTER the .bazelversion 8.2.1 convergence
# PR merged, and that commit records .bazelversion 8.2.1 -- so the pinned
# registry commit agrees with the estate-bazelversion line below. Every future
# SHA bump repeats the same discipline: bump with the refresh one-liner above,
# regenerate MODULE.bazel.lock in the SAME commit (a re-pin rewrites every
# registry URL key in it, 161 keys), and re-read the registry's .bazelversion
# at the new commit to confirm it still records the estate value below.
#
# estate-bazelversion: 8.2.1
#   The estate-wide Bazel version. It is the value recorded by the registry's
#   own .bazelversion at the commit pinned below, read at that commit when
#   this pin was taken. scripts/scaffold-doctor-boundary.sh asserts root
#   .bazelversion equals this value (offline). See "LIMITS" in that script:
#   it proves this repo has not drifted from the value recorded here, NOT that
#   the pinned registry commit still records the same value. Only re-reading
#   the registry at the pinned SHA proves that, which is why it is a step of
#   the re-pin procedure above rather than a check this repo can run offline.
#
# The estate-wide Bazel version SSOT, the two-registry chain, and this pin
# convention are specified in that registry's own docs, not here (this link
# tracks the registry's default branch and does not need re-pinning):
#   https://github.com/tinyland-inc/bazel-registry/blob/main/docs/bazel-adoption-v0.md
common --registry=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tinyland-inc/bazel-registry/ef734c4a26045a7b396913e6cf410e50fbe16635
# bcr stays as a secondary registry; the Tinyland registry stays first so
# in-house Bazel modules resolve before falling through to bcr.bazel.build.
common --registry=https://bcr.bazel.build

# Local graph inspection only. Product actions execute through the compiled v4
# client and its controller-resolved REAPI binding; this file carries no cache,
# executor, endpoint, profile, or fallback authority.
build --jobs=auto
build --worker_sandboxing
build --keep_going
build --show_timestamps

# rules_ts: skip lib check is required for SvelteKit-style declaration files.
build --@aspect_rules_ts//ts:skipLibCheck=always
build --spawn_strategy=sandboxed,worker
# Local developer builds use Bazel's internal CopyFile action to materialize
# rules_js runfiles; that bookkeeping mnemonic has no Darwin sandbox
# implementation. Protected v4 actions do not read this file: the compiled
# gf-action-client invokes Bazel with --ignore_all_rc_files. A later
# --spawn_strategy cannot override this mnemonic-specific setting, so any
# change to that client boundary requires a fresh execution-policy review.
build --strategy=CopyFile=local

# Test output
test --test_output=errors
test --test_summary=detailed
test --test_verbose_timeout_warnings
test --test_timeout=120,600,1800,3600
